-- A line in the form of a mixfix rule with a bare name for every input has no
-- literal to tell it from a definition, so it is read as one: of a rule named
-- Red with the inputs `costs` and n. It checked, and `Red `costs` 0` went on
-- giving the one definition's answer, 0, where the line meant 1. It is refused,
-- once, at the line (found by the pre-review of legalese/l4-ide#545,
-- 2026-10-13).
DECLARE Colour IS ONE OF Red, Green, Blue

GIVEN c IS A Colour
      n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
c `costs` n MEANS n
Red `costs` n MEANS 1

#EVAL Red `costs` 0
#EVAL Green `costs` 5
